        description {The link command is used within the body of a method, constructor, or destructor to create a command in the object's own private namespace that invokes a method on the current object. Each linkName is either a plain name (aliasing to the method of the same name) or a two-element list {linkName targetName} aliasing linkName to a differently-named method.}
